OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real,
compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by the merged
predecessor `page:automations/AutomationActivityFeed` (and every other DONE P7 page, e.g.
Analytics/StatisticsPage, Admin/ApiPlaygroundPage). `Sources` is a project.yml source path
(createIntermediateGroups), shared by the iOS + macOS app targets (ADR-002). The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9.

REUSE (DRY, in-module, public — not a predecessor bypass):
The web ConditionBuilder's pure domain model + payload-coercion ladder + the `useGeofences`
state-holder seam already exist as PUBLIC, module-level types from the P4 surface
`TeslaSync/feature-views/ConditionBuilder.*`. To avoid redeclaration collisions and duplication,
this P7 page REUSES (references, does not modify) the value types
(`AutomationConditionInput`, `ConditionBody`, `SignalCondition`/`TimeWindowCondition`/
`GeofenceCondition`/`OtherAutomationCondition`, the kind/op/state enums, `SignalField`), the pure
`ConditionBuilderAdapter` (web `createDefaultCondition`/`conditionValueFromInput`/operator filter/
`numericValue`/`parseFloat||0`/`parseInt||0`/`toggleDay`/geofence + timezone projections + the
SIGNAL_FIELDS / COMMON_TIMEZONES / DAYS catalogs), and the geofence `useGeofences` seam
(`GeofenceOptionsModel`, `GeofencePresentation`, `GeofenceOption`, `GeofenceOptionsSource`,
`InMemoryGeofenceOptionsSource`, `GeofenceLoadState`). It does NOT reuse the P4 `CBStrings` facade:
that resolves from a SEPARATE per-surface `ConditionBuilder.strings` table, while THIS prompt
requires `Localizable.xcstrings`. So the entire VIEW layer (page + row + 4 field editors + geofence
picker) is self-contained and renders catalog keys via `LocalizedStringKey` (no hardcoded English).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `ConditionBuilder` is a controlled section the `/automations` builder renders inline (the
`{ conditions, onChange }` form) — NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level
`AppRoute` (that would hijack the builder's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination`
seam — `ConditionBuilderLink` + `View.conditionBuilderDestination()` +
`ConditionBuilderRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link the
full editor. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) or any sibling surface were
made — correct for an unrouted unit and consistent with the predecessor-bypass rule (covenant #7).

